From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:42:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 121/128] render: a sorted 3D scene runs its text scripts in
 the scene's object order

A text layer's script runs as the layer draws. Since transparentsorting draws WE's two passes (0119), every text is in
the translucent list, sorted far to near, so its script ran in that order instead of the scene's. 3509243656's
`userset` text (listed late, far out) then ran before its `time` text (listed early, near) on the first frame and read
shared.xntime before `time` had set it: "TypeError: cannot read property 'toExponential' of undefined", a degraded
scene in the health report. Under transparentsorting the text scripts now run first, in the scene's object order, and
each text draws what its script returned. Inferred: WE runs a text's script in its update, not in the renderer's
sorted passes (not traced in wallpaper64.exe); a scene without the sort is unchanged.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-health.md (3509243656 degraded by the 0119 pin: a first-frame script error)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
